      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2723357819,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "For hf_ieee80211_he_trigger_type, we only add 1 byte. Also the definition is u64 with mask. So there is no problem to use ENC_NA.\n\nWarning: epan/dissectors/packet-ieee80211.c:14675 proto_tree_add_item called for FT_UINT32 field \"hf_ieee80211_tag_length\"  - with bad encoding - \"ENC_NA\" - {'ENC_BIG_ENDIAN', 'ENC_LITTLE_ENDIAN', 'ENC_HOST_ENDIAN'} allowed\nIn 14675, we also only add 1 byte for hf_ieee80211_tag_length. ENC_NA is OK.\n\nShould we detect similar warnings with better detection? Or we just use little endian to skip the waring?",
          "author": {
            "id": 14135780,
            "username": "WFA-achuang",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Albert Chuang",
