          "id": 2723636795,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Warning: epan/dissectors/packet-ieee80211.c:21818 proto_tree_add_item_ret_uint called for FT_UINT16 field \"hf_ieee80211_vs_sgdsn_heading\"  - with bad encoding - \"ENC_NA\" - {'ENC_BIG_ENDIAN', 'ENC_LITTLE_ENDIAN', 'ENC_HOST_ENDIAN'} allowed\nWarning: epan/dissectors/packet-ieee80211.c:21790 proto_tree_add_item_ret_int called for FT_INT32 field \"hf_ieee80211_vs_sgdsn_gpscoord\"  - with bad encoding - \"ENC_NA\" - {'ENC_BIG_ENDIAN', 'ENC_LITTLE_ENDIAN', 'ENC_HOST_ENDIAN'} allowed\nWarning: epan/dissectors/packet-ieee80211.c:21800 proto_tree_add_item_ret_int called for FT_INT16 field \"hf_ieee80211_vs_sgdsn_altitude\"  - with bad encoding - \"ENC_NA\" - {'ENC_BIG_ENDIAN', 'ENC_LITTLE_ENDIAN', 'ENC_HOST_ENDIAN'} allowed\n\nThese three fields are vendor specific. I am not sure this is OK to use little endian.",
          "author": {
            "id": 14135780,
            "username": "WFA-achuang",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Albert Chuang",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
